Here is a concise system overview focused on the **smart contract connection**.

# Smart Contract Connection to the System

The smart contract serves as the **trusted reward layer** of the application. It is not responsible for gameplay or business logic—it only executes and records verified rewards on Avalanche.

## System Flow

```text
Frontend
    │
    │ Connect Wallet
    ▼
Backend
    │
    │ Store rider wallet address
    ▼
Database (Supabase)
    │
    │ Rider completes delivery
    ▼
Gamification Engine
    │
    │ Calculates:
    │ • XP
    │ • Levels
    │ • Missions
    │ • Reputation
    │ • Reward Eligibility
    ▼
Reward Service
    │
    │ If rewardEligible == true
    ▼
Avalanche Smart Contract
    │
    │ Uses backend credentials (.env):
    │ • PRIVATE_KEY
    │ • RPC_URL
    │ • CONTRACT_ADDRESS
    │
    │ Executes:
    │ • Reward payout
    │ • Achievement recording
    │ • Emits blockchain event
    ▼
Avalanche Network
    │
    │ Returns Transaction Hash
    ▼
Backend
    │
    │ Stores txHash and reward record
    ▼
Frontend
    │
    │ Displays reward confirmation,
    │ updated progress, and blockchain transaction link.
```

## Responsibilities

### Frontend

* Connect the rider's wallet.
* Send the wallet address to the backend.
* Display gameplay progress and blockchain transaction status.

### Backend

* Manage the game engine.
* Determine reward eligibility.
* Securely sign blockchain transactions using the server's private key.
* Communicate with the Avalanche smart contract.

### Smart Contract

* Receive reward requests from the backend.
* Transfer rewards to rider wallets.
* Record achievements or reward events on-chain.
* Return a verifiable transaction hash.

### Avalanche

Provides a transparent, immutable record of rewards and achievements, ensuring payouts can be independently verified while keeping gameplay fast by processing game logic off-chain.
